  "body": "## What\n\nStores the shared `epoch` counter on `globalThis.nanostores` instead of as a plain module-level variable. This ensures all module instances of nanostores share the same epoch counter, regardless of how they are bundled.\n\n## Why\n\nWhen nanostores is bundled separately in different parts of an application (e.g., tree-shaking separates core from React, or Turbopack creates multiple module instances — see https://github.com/nanostores/nanostores/issues/371#issuecomment-2098405189), each bundle can end up with its own `epoch` instance. This causes `computed` stores to not receive updates from `atom` stores in different bundles, because the epoch counters are independent and never sync.\n\n## How\n\nThe fix stores `epoch` on `globalThis.nanostores` (a shared namespace object) before exporting it:\n\n\n\nThis approach:\n1. Uses `globalThis` as a truly global storage (not affected by bundler tree-shaking)\n2. Creates a shared `nanostores` namespace on `globalThis` to avoid polluting the global namespace\n3. Initializes `epoch` only if not already present (safe for multiple module instances)\n4. Maintains the same `export let epoch` API so no changes needed elsewhere\n\n## Testing\n\nAll 46 existing tests pass with this change.\n\nCloses #371",
